From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] board: sunxi: Avaota A1: mux SPI0 NAND pins on Port J

The Avaota A1 SPI NAND (Winbond W25N01GV) is wired to SPI0 on Port J
(PJ20-CS0, PJ21-CLK, PJ22-MOSI, PJ23-MISO, PJ25-WP, PJ26-HOLD), which
needs pinmux 5. The A523 pinctrl table in U-Boot only knows SPI0 on
Port C (pinmux 4), so the DT cannot express the Port J muxing. Set it
explicitly here. This runs in the SPL and the muxing persists into
U-Boot proper.

Signed-off-by: Armbian Build Framework <build@armbian.com>
Signed-off-by: Juan Sanchez Fuentes <juanesf91@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: opencode:big-pickle
---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index da307bf..7445a42 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -683,6 +683,31 @@ void sunxi_board_init(void)
 	power_failed |= axp_set_sw(IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_AXP_SW_ON));
 #endif
 #endif	/* CONFIG_AXPxxx_POWER */
+
+	/*
+	 * The Avaota A1 SPI NAND (Winbond W25N01GV) is wired to SPI0 on
+	 * Port J (PJ20-CS0, PJ21-CLK, PJ22-MOSI, PJ23-MISO, PJ25-WP,
+	 * PJ26-HOLD), which needs pinmux 5. The A523 pinctrl table in
+	 * U-Boot only knows SPI0 on Port C (pinmux 4), so the DT cannot
+	 * express the Port J muxing. Set it explicitly here (this runs in
+	 * the SPL, and the muxing persists into U-Boot proper), matching
+	 * the kernel DT (allwinner,pinmux = <5>).
+	 */
+#if defined(CONFIG_MACH_SUN55I_A523) && IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SPI_SUNXI)
+	{
+		/* Port J is bank 9; SUNXI_GPIO_J is not defined for older SoCs */
+		void *pj = (void *)SUNXI_PIO_BASE +
+			   (SUNXI_GPIO_I + 1) * SUNXI_PINCTRL_BANK_SIZE;
+
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgbank(pj, 20, 5);	/* PJ20 SPI0-CS0 */
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgbank(pj, 21, 5);	/* PJ21 SPI0-CLK */
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgbank(pj, 22, 5);	/* PJ22 SPI0-MOSI */
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgbank(pj, 23, 5);	/* PJ23 SPI0-MISO */
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgbank(pj, 25, 5);	/* PJ25 SPI0-WP */
+		sunxi_gpio_set_cfgbank(pj, 26, 5);	/* PJ26 SPI0-HOLD */
+	}
+#endif
+
 	printf("DRAM:");
 	gd->ram_size = sunxi_dram_init();
 	printf(" %d MiB\n", (int)(gd->ram_size >> 20));
